hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16085","He said, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, he said, Salamah ibn al-Fadl al-Ansari narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said, Sad ibn Tariq al-Ashjai, and he is Abu Malik, narrated to me, from Salamah ibn Nuaym ibn Masud al-Ashjai, from his father Nuaym, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, when he read the letter of Musaylimah the liar, he said to the two messengers: So what do you two say. They said, we say as he said. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, were it not that messengers are not killed, I would have struck your necks."
